FreeRusch is an independent, clean-room implementation of the Rüsch method for
bridge slab design. It does not include, link to, or copy code or data from
commercial software. T-Rüsch (TQS) is referenced only as a functional
description of the engineering domain, never as a source.

Normative references

The Brazilian standards NBR 7188:2013 and NBR 6118:2023 are cited as engineering
references. Their text is not distributed with this software, and no excerpt of
them is reproduced in the source tree.

Third-party material

The embedded Rüsch coefficient tables come from an academic workbook whose
provenance, checksum and extraction procedure are recorded in ATTRIBUTION.md.
Runtime dependencies are listed there as well.

The FreeRusch name and logo are not covered by the licenses above.
